      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In November 1926 the Fairfield Beach Property Owners Association was founded, once boasting 216 members who hosted dances and community clean‑ups.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://escapetobuckeyelake.com/directory/fairfield-beach/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fairfield Beach sits on Buckeye Lake’s largest public shoreline, featuring a sand beach, picnic area, and boat ramp.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://escapetobuckeyelake.com/directory/fairfield-beach/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "What began as a seasonal retreat has evolved into a vibrant, year‑round community, now the most populous unincorporated neighborhood in the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://escapetobuckeyelake.com/directory/fairfield-beach/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Fairfield Beach lies 4 miles northwest of Thornville and 33 miles east of downtown Columbus, placing it within easy reach of the state capital.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
